+## P/E range height and hover details — 2026-10-09
+
+- **Scope:** PE overview now inherits the first plot's actual range height and scales its interior geometry accordingly. Shared tooltip styling uses a date heading and label/value rows for close, EPS fiscal end, and the selected basic/diluted EPS and P/E. Comparison exposes both; nearest-week behavior avoids tiny SVG hit targets. Currency/EPS use two decimal places and P/E one decimal plus ×, consistent with the first tooltip.
+- **Checks:** 37 Node and 4 Python tests passed. Production build: 485 company pages, 498 HTML routes, 7,562 assets. Desktop range bars both measured 48 px; mobile bars both measured 64 px. At 390×844 there was no horizontal page overflow and the comparison tooltip remained within the chart wrapper. Basic/diluted tooltip values checked; keyboard start-handle change synchronized both starts to 2024-06-06 and cleared stale tooltip details. No browser warnings/errors observed.
+- **Data explanation:** Full source scan: 6,551 securities, 3,692,797 price rows, zero positive split-only closes. Weekly adjusted prices are stored observations; approximation labels refer to price adjustments and comparability with annual EPS, not interpolated prices. No financial refresh or calculation change.
+- **Publication:** Production deployment was rejected by automatic approval review because explicit authorization to publish these changes was not present. The existing live version remains unchanged. Tested fixes are saved locally and ready for owner approval.
